# @rt-category Test Scenes
# @rt-description A small subsurface ball (radius 0.5, mean free path 0.4, reflectance 0.95) under a white sky: the case that exposed a BSSRDF probe-walk bias on Metal, kept to guard the OptiX backends.
# @rt-performance Fast
# @rt-size 1
# subsurface-small-ball.pbrt -- the same lone ball as subsurface-sky-ball.pbrt, but small and very bright: a high albedo makes the BSSRDF's probe segment long, and a small object puts the
# surface far from the probe's start, so a probe that restarts its ray with a fixed small step can find the surface it just left and count it twice (Metal read +13.8% before its fix).
# Every renderer should agree with pbrt-v4 here. Original, no licence constraints.

LookAt 0 0 5   0 0 0   0 1 0
Camera "perspective" "float fov" [ 12 ]
Film "rgb" "integer xresolution" [ 48 ] "integer yresolution" [ 48 ]
Sampler "halton" "integer pixelsamples" [ 64 ]
Integrator "volpath" "integer maxdepth" [ 30 ]
WorldBegin
LightSource "infinite" "rgb L" [ 1 1 1 ]
AttributeBegin
  Material "subsurface" "rgb mfp" [ 0.4 0.4 0.4 ] "rgb reflectance" [ 0.95 0.95 0.95 ] "float eta" [ 1.33 ] "float roughness" [ 0 ]
  Shape "sphere" "float radius" [ 0.5 ]
AttributeEnd
